{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB04572 - MONDO_18369",
  "verbalization": "Thiotepa, a chemotherapy agent, is linked to Immature Ovarian Teratoma through a chain of indications involving Cisplatin. The evidence suggests that Thiotepa may be associated with the development or progression of ovarian tumors, as it is indicated for conditions such as Malignant Dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor of Ovary, Familial Ovarian Cancer, and Malignant Sex Cord Stromal Tumor of Ovary, all of which are linked to Cisplatin. Cisplatin, in turn, is indicated for Immature Ovarian Teratoma, indicating a potential mechanistic or pathophysiological connection between Thiotepa and the tumor. The shared use of Cisplatin in these contexts suggests a possible indirect relationship, possibly involving the role of Cisplatin in the treatment or pathogenesis of these ovarian tumors. The evidence supports a pathway where Thiotepa may influence the development of Immature Ovarian Teratoma through its interaction with Cisplatin, though the exact mechanism remains unclear.",
